{
  "description": "How the gateway's decision routes (/v1/systemone, /v1/decisions) check a request's envelope and map a vendor's answer onto the gateway's error table. Read by the gateway's Go tests (agentcc-gateway/internal/models/decision_test.go, internal/providers/systemone/systemone_test.go, internal/server/handlers_decision_test.go) and the Jev client's Python tests (futureagi/ee/jev/tests/test_client.py), so the two sides cannot drift apart unnoticed. Hand-written, not generated. envelope_cases: a body and either the format and questions the gateway reads from it, or the 400/422 it returns; no error may echo must_not_echo. error_cases: what a vendor answers to request (sent with api_key) and what the gateway returns; returned.retry_after is the Retry-After it passes on, and the x-agentcc-upstream-status header carries upstream.status. gateway_error_cases: refusals the gateway makes before calling any vendor.",
